{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reversed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/reversed"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/reversed"},"abstract":[{"text":"Every column’s sources and targets swapped, every entry negated (a vertex on both sides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stays 0): Gallo et al.’s symmetric image. An involution. O(1): the planes swap.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reversed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","title":"reversed","roleHeading":"Instance Property","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V8reversedACvp","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L465"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"role":"collection","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/reversed":{"abstract":[{"text":"Every column’s sources and targets swapped, every entry negated (a vertex on both sides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stays 0): Gallo et al.’s symmetric image. An involution. O(1): the planes swap.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/reversed","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/reversed","title":"reversed","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}}}